PROBLEM STATEMENT:
You are given a list of student information: ID, FirstName, and CGPA.
Your task is to rearrange the students according to the following rules:
Sort by CGPA in decreasing order.
If two students have the same CGPA, sort them by FirstName in alphabetical order.
If both CGPA and FirstName are the same, sort them by ID in ascending order.
Finally, print the FirstName of each student in the sorted order.
AIM:
To implement a program in Java that uses a Comparator to sort a list of student objects based on multiple criteria (CGPA, FirstName, ID) and display the sorted names.
JAVA CODE:
import java.util.*;
class Student {
    int id;
    String firstName;
    double cgpa;

    Student(int id, String firstName, double cgpa) {
        this.id = id;
        this.firstName = firstName;
        this.cgpa = cgpa;
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int svg = sc.nextInt();  // number of students
        List<Student> students = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < svg; i++) {
            int id = sc.nextInt();
            String name = sc.next();
            double cgpa = sc.nextDouble();
            students.add(new Student(id, name, cgpa));
        }

        // Sorting using custom comparator
        students.sort((s1, s2) -> {
            if (Double.compare(s2.cgpa, s1.cgpa) != 0) {
                return Double.compare(s2.cgpa, s1.cgpa); // Higher CGPA first
            } else if (!s1.firstName.equals(s2.firstName)) {
                return s1.firstName.compareTo(s2.firstName); // Alphabetical order
            } else {
                return Integer.compare(s1.id, s2.id); // Smaller ID first
            }
        });

        // Printing result
        for (Student s : students) {
            System.out.println(s.firstName);
        }
    }
}
